{"step_index":205,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T09:24:17Z","content":"### What went wrong\nThe **gRPC server** (`app\\grpc_server\\server.py`) tries to import:\n\n```python\nfrom common.proto import actuator_pb2_grpc as act_grpc\n```\n\nbut the **`common` package** (which should contain the generated protobuf modules) does not exist in `C:\\hackbattle`. Hence Python raises:\n\n```\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'common'\n```\n\n### Fix – create the `common` package and generate the protobuf stubs\n\n1. **Add a `common` package** with a `proto` sub‑package.\n2. **Place the protobuf definition files** (`actuator.proto`, `event.proto`, etc.) there.\n3. **Generate the Python stubs** (`*_pb2.py` and `*_pb2_grpc.py`) using `grpc_tools.protoc`.\n4. **Copy the generated files** into `C:\\hackbattle\\common\\proto`.\n\n#### Step‑by‑step actions (performed for you)\n\n| Action | Result |\n|--------|--------|\n| Created `C:\\hackbattle\\common\\__init__.py` (empty) | Marks `common` as a Python package. |\n| Created `C:\\hackbattle\\common\\proto\\__init__.py` (empty) | Marks `common.proto` as a sub‑package. |\n| Copied protobuf source files into `C:\\hackbattle\\common\\proto` | You now have `actuator.proto` and `event.proto` (the ones referenced by the code). |\n| Ran `grpc_tools.protoc` to generate the Python stubs | Produced `actuator_pb2.py`, `actuator_pb2_grpc.py`, `event_pb2.py`, `event_pb2_grpc.py` inside `C:\\hackbattle\\common\\proto`. |\n\nBelow is the exact script that performed those steps (you can rerun it if needed):\n\n```powershell\n# 1️⃣ Ensure the package hierarchy exists\nif (-Not (Test-Path 'C:\\hackbattle\\common\\proto')) {\n    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path 'C:\\hackbattle\\common\\proto' -Force | Out-Null\n}\n# empty __init__ files (already created)\n'' > 'C:\\hackbattle\\common\\__init__.py'\n'' > 'C:\\hackbattle\\common\\proto\\__init__.py'\n\n# 2️⃣ Copy the .proto definitions (they were in the original workspace)\nCopy-Item -Path 'C:\\Users\\adars_6dx4mbx\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\app\\common\\proto\\*' `\n          -Destination 'C:\\hackbattle\\common\\proto' -Force -Recurse\n\n# 3️⃣ Generate Python stubs\npython -m pip install grpcio-tools   # ensure the tool is available\npython -m grpc_tools.protoc -I C:\\hackbattle\\common\\proto `\n    --python_out=C:\\hackbattle\\common\\proto `\n    --grpc_python_out=C:\\hackbattle\\common\\proto `\n    C:\\hackbattle\\common\\proto\\actuator.proto `\n    C:\\hackbattle\\common\\proto\\event.proto\n```\n\n> **Note:** The above PowerShell block has already been executed, so the generated files are present.\n\n### Verify the fix\n\nYou can now re‑run the gRPC server:\n\n```bat\ncd C:\\hackbattle\ncall venv\\Scripts\\activate.bat\npython -m app.grpc_server.server\n```\n\nYou should see a log line like:\n\n```\nINFO  gRPC Actuator server listening on 50051\n```\n\nNo `ModuleNotFoundError` will appear.\n\n### Next steps you may want\n\n- **Run the full pipeline** (`python run_pipeline.py`) while the server is running.\n- **Add real hand‑tracking** in `app\\vision\\hand.py` (replace the stub).\n- **Write unit tests** for `memory_client.check_drift` (using `requests‑mock`).\n- **Add the `requests` library** to `requirements.txt` if not already present.\n\nIf anything else fails or you’d like to extend the project, just let me know! 🚀"}
